{"name":"Blueberry Soda","hex":"#8290a6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blueberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible round berry, belonging to the cowberry group (Vaccinium sect. Cyanococcus), with flared crowns at the end, that turns blue on ripening.","The shrub of the above-mentioned berry."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark blue colour.","Resembling or characteristic of blueberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blueberry"},{"term":"soda","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sodium bicarbonate.","Sodium carbonate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soda"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blueberry","blocks":[{"text":"Blueberries are a widely distributed and widespread group of perennial flowering plants with blue or purple berries. They are classified in the section Cyanococcus within the genus Vaccinium. Commercial blueberries—both wild (lowbush) and cultivated (highbush)—are all native to North America. The highbush varieties were introduced into Europe during the 1930s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Blueberries.jpg/330px-Blueberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blueberry","wikidata":"Q13178"},{"title":"Soft drink","blocks":[{"text":"A soft drink is a class of beverage containing no alcohol, usually carbonated, and typically including added sweetener. Flavors can be natural, artificial or a mixture of the two. The sweetener may be a sugar, high-fructose corn syrup, fruit juice, a sugar substitute, or some combination of these. Soft drinks may also contain caffeine, colorings, preservatives and other ingredients. Soft drinks are called \"soft\" in contrast with \"hard\" alcoholic drinks and non-alcoholic drinks. Small amounts of alcohol may be present in a soft drink, but the alcohol content must be less than 0.5% of the total volume of the drink (ABV) in many countries and localities if the drink is to not be considered alcoholic. Examples of soft drinks include lemon-lime drinks, orange soda, cola, grape soda, cream soda, ginger ale and root beer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Tumbler_of_cola_with_ice.jpg/330px-Tumbler_of_cola_with_ice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_drink","wikidata":"Q147538"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/1280px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blueberries showing various stages of maturation. IG = Immature Green, GP = Green Pink, BP = Blue Pink, and R = Ripe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg/500px-Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg/1280px-Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg/500px-Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Whole blueberry and in cross-section","link":"http